      "location": "Diaspora",
      "country": "Syria",
      "names": "Niazi Haidar, Nazem Bek Sanjer, Jawad Anzor, Tawfiq Kabartai, Kamal Qushha, Kamel Bek, Haider bek, Tawfiq Anzor, Amin Anzor, Safou Qushha.",
      "dignitaries": "Jawad Talostan Anzor",
      "dignitaryBorn": "1900",
      "dignitaryDied": "1948",
      "tribe": "Kabardian/Kabartai/Kabardey",
      "inscription": "Sidenote",
      "inscriptionLanguage": "Arabic",
      "notes": "The Circassian Cavalry Corps in Syria was established in the 1920s. There were 15 squadrons of Circassian cavalry, of which three were motorized, each with about a hundred cavaliers. They were led by Circassian officers and non-commissioned officers with a small cadre of French officers. The overall leader of the Corps was French colonel Philibert Collet. The Corps was disbanded in 1946, upon independence of Syria.",
      "context": {
